Hi Heather,

Could we talk about a six-session workplace meetings course for 24 of our sta=
ff? I would like people to be able to read an agenda and make a short proposa=
l that gives the chair something clear to decide.

At our operations meeting we spent time explaining the repair handover under =
item 3, but found it difficult to move from that update to the decision in it=
em 4. People had useful information, yet it was not always clear what they wa=
nted the meeting to decide. Could the practice include saying that request fi=
rst, before giving the supporting detail?

I've attached the agenda extract as a possible starting point. Would you be a=
vailable at 10:00 a.m. on Thursday, August 22, to discuss the group and what =
the sessions might cover?

Thanks,
Glenn

Glenn Fletcher
Rosedale Workers Housing Cooperative

